{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297533-concept-heterodoxical-styles-featuring-cloud-mastery-style-and-golden-bells-style","id":1297533,"title":"Concept- Heterodoxical Styles (Featuring Cloud Mastery Style and Golden Bells Style)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-17T10:37:53-07:00","id":1297533,"title":"Concept- Heterodoxical Styles (Featuring Cloud Mastery Style and Golden Bells Style)","content":"(Because I'm not above stealing directly from other games)<br /> <br /> <br /> Across Creation, ten thousand schools of martial arts practice, and no two are precisely the same. Secret techniques and bitter rivalries can tear apart a temple that has stood united for a hundred years, and masters pass down minor variations that outsiders could barely distinguish from the parent style.<br /> <br /> Typically, these differences are too minor to be differentiated mechanically. But in some cases, styles will grow wild and strange when transplanted into foreign soils. Such is the case with the Immaculate Martial Arts and the Pure Way of Prasad. Although they are very similar, deviations and heresies have led to some... unusual approaches. Aproaches that often lead to duels, demonstrating the superiority of the orthodox or the heterodox.<br /> <br /> To learn both the original and heterodoxical styles, a Martial Artist must buy up her ability in both styles independently, but need not repurchase charms to act as prerequisites. A Martial Artist who can gain Mastery benefits from Martial Arts can learn both orthodox and heterodox charms without buying the second style up. Tthe Heterodox keyword denotes charms that differ from the parent style, and which charm it replaces.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <b>Cloud Mastery Style</b><br /> <i>Heterodoxical Air Dragon Style</i><br /> <br /> Clouds and fog are like the gods; present yet intangible, sometimes sailing lazily through the heavens and other times all around you upon the earth. Cloud Mastery allows monks of the Pure Way to become as the clouds, and thus, to become as the gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Moon Covered By Clouds</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 3i, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Air, Heterodox<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Air Dragon Sight<br /> <br /> With wide sweeping arm movements, the martial artist draws a heavy shroud of fog across the battlefield the same way others might don a cloak, drawing it behind her as she moves. Until the end of the scene, this heavy fog billows out to short range from her, imposing a penalty of (Essence) on movement and visual actions (including most attacks and defenses), and grants concealment for establishing surprise.<br /> <br /> In Air Aura, the martial artist also ignores up to (Essence) of these penalties; while students can dim the sky, masters seem to turn day into murky night.<br /> <br /> Moon Covered By Clouds is Heterodoxical with Breath-Seizing Technique<br /> <br /> <b>Phantom of the Clouds</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m, 1wp, expend Air Aura; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute, Perilous, Decisive-only, Air, Heterodox<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Thunderclap Kata<br /> <br /> To strike a cloud is more futile than to battle the sea, for tides and rivers may be directed by great earthworks but only the gods command the sky. Upon being struck by a decisive attack, the martial artist may use Phantom of the Clouds, rolling (Dexterity + Essence) and negating one level of damage with each success. If this reduces the attack to zero damage, it is considered to have missed and the martial artist may make a reflexive attempt to enter stealth. Phantom of the Clouds may only be used once a day, unless reset by building to 10+ initiative over the highest opponent.<br /> <br /> Phantom of the Clouds is Heterodoxical with Wrathful Winds Kiai<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Temple Bells Style</b><br /> <i>Heterodoxical Earth Dragon Style</i><br /> <br /> Named for the golden bells that call the people of Prasad to prayer, the monks of the Pure Way practice inuring themselves to the harshest of blows, striking with impossible force, and leaving her opponents shaken and his ears ringing.<br /> <br /> <b>Hardness of the Bell</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Earth, Perilous, Heterodox<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Stone Dragon's Skin<br /> <br /> To strike a Golden Temple Bell is to be struck, as the reverberation echoes back through the attacker's arms and numbs her palms. Hardness of the Bell increases her Hardness by (Stamina) against one attack and inflict a -1 onslaught penalty until his next action. Withering attacks that do less damage than her Hardness before they are soaked, or decisive attacks that do not overcome her Hardness, also drain (Essence) initiative from the attacker. The martial artist does not gain this initiative, it is simply lost.<br /> <br /> In Earth Aura, the martial artist gains (Essence/2) of the stolen initiative.<br /> <br /> Hardness of the Bell is Heterodoxical with Unmoving Mountain Stance.<br /> <br /> <b>Army-Rattling Peals of the Bell</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (+4m, 1wp); <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Heterodox, Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique<br /> <br /> When the golden bells of Prasad ring out, all fall to their knees in supplication and prayer. Army-Rattling Peals of the Bell enhances Hardness of the Bell; if the martial artist spends an additional 4 motes and 1 willpower when using Hardness of the Bell her defense is enhanced; in addition to rattling her attacker, she rings out with a powerful pulse upon being struck, rocking all near her. If she was struck by a withering attack, she rolls (Stamina + Martial Arts) once as a smashing counterattack against all opponents at close range, with a base damage equal to the raw damage of the attack that struck her. If she was struck by a decisive attack, the ring becomes deadly, allowing her to make a decisive counterattack of (Stamina + Martial Arts) against all opponents within close range, evenly dividing her initiative among them. Army-Rattling Peals of the Bell may not be used in response to a counterattack.<br /> <br /> Army-Rattling Peals of the Bell is Heterodoxical with Avalanche Method.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T10:43:12-07:00","id":1297535,"title":"","content":"I fully endorse stealing from Weapons of the gods for martial arts and encourage more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T11:38:55-07:00","id":1297545,"title":"","content":"Hardness of the Bell: This charm, as written, stacks with armor meaning it\u2019s pretty trivially easy to get Hardness 16 with this charm\u2014 this is quite high\u2014 also depending on how it\u2019s written it will basically automatically crash any character who hits the Martial artist with a Decisive Attack once she has Essence 3+ that deals less than hardness damage as most characters will reset to Initiative 3 and then lose 3i, if the drain occurs before reseting then this is fine but does very little, if it occurs after it feels strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:03:32-07:00","id":1297551,"title":"","content":"Hm. Maybe, +3; +4 if you're in medium armor, +5 if you're in light armor, and +6 if you're unarmored","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:23:01-07:00","id":1297557,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t quite understand your notation. Maybe a Decisive soak effect though? Like roll (Stamina+Essence) when hit, for each success reduce damage dice by -1 before hardness, in earth aura up to (Essence) 10s on this roll each add +1 to hardness. An attack from close range which lands but deals no damage inflicts onslaught on the attacker and is treated as having missed, the attacker loses 1i more Initiative per point by which the attack failed to meet her hardness, maximum (Essence). The Martial Artist may add half this Initiative, round up, to each damage roll of Army Rattling Peals of The bell if she uses it to make a Decisive Attack in response. Otherwise it is lost.<br /> <br /> Or if that feels strong you could have the stamina+Essence roll be at a difficulty of half the threshold successes on the attack roll with extra successes reducing damage by -1 dice each. <br /> <br /> Just spitballing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 03-17-2019, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T14:31:33-07:00","id":1297584,"title":"","content":"Bah, that'll teach me to try and post from my phone &gt;&lt;<br /> <br /> What I was trying to capture was answering the 'Hardness of the Bell lets you get to Hardness 16 trivially' by suggesting it only adds +3 Hardness base, with increasing amounts of Hardness if you are in lighter armor - so, +4 if you are in Medium armor, +5 if you are in Light armor, and +6 if you are unarmored.<br /> <br /> The ease of crashing people at base initiative is a good point I hadn't fully thought through. Imma revise that to 'reduce initiative by Essence / 2' and make it clear that if the decisive attack fails because of the increase in hardness it is treated as a miss.<br /> <br /> I definitely *don't* want it to be a 'reduce decisive damage with Hardness' thing. Earth is strong until it shatters; bells ring until they crack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic 